From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: System Electronics <ci@sysele.local>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Support/Signals.h: add missing <cstdint> include for GCC 13

GCC 13's libstdc++ no longer transitively pulls in <cstdint> via
<string>, so the use of uintptr_t in CleanupOnSignal() fails to
compile with:

  error: 'uintptr_t' was not declared in this scope

Matches the fix applied upstream in later LLVM releases (e.g.
llvm-project commit adding missing standard header includes for
GCC 13 compatibility).

Upstream-Status: Backport
Signed-off-by: System Electronics <ci@sysele.local>
---
 llvm/include/llvm/Support/Signals.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/llvm/include/llvm/Support/Signals.h b/llvm/include/llvm/Support/Signals.h
--- a/llvm/include/llvm/Support/Signals.h
+++ b/llvm/include/llvm/Support/Signals.h
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #ifndef LLVM_SUPPORT_SIGNALS_H
 #define LLVM_SUPPORT_SIGNALS_H

+#include <cstdint>
 #include <string>

 namespace llvm {
--
2.34.1
